soju-tui for Debian and Ubuntu
================================

The package installs the interactive command as /usr/bin/soju-tui. It does not
start a daemon, change Soju, grant administrative access, or install a
soju-tui systemd service.

The administrator who should use the TUI must already be able to write Soju's
administrative Unix socket. On a systemd host, explicitly run the packaged
guided helper after installation:

  sudo soju-tui-setup --user LOGIN

The helper previews and confirms a narrowly scoped ACL for the selected local
account, verifies sojuctl access, and installs a path unit that reapplies that
ACL only when Soju recreates its administrative socket.

A manually installed /usr/local/bin/soju-tui usually takes precedence over the
packaged /usr/bin/soju-tui. Use `type -a soju-tui` to find every copy, and move
or remove the manual copy before relying on package upgrades.
